{
  "abstract": "Over half of known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. Parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$ makes the regular fifths linear in $S_{ab}$ and completes the square in all three remaining conditions, cutting out the Branch-1 and twin-fifth sextuple surfaces. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and the first rational almost septuple of relation type $(5,2)$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness on $H$ by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. Varying the base quadruple via Master Syzygies yields the universal osculating surface ($18/21$-compatible over $w_1(q)=(q^2-3)/(2q)$, with four $19/21$ branches $\\Lambda\\in V_4\\cdot w_1$) and the QRT Vieta-jumping tower $Q_{n-1}=[n]P_\\infty\\oplus T_0$ on the Weierstrass cubic $E_W(R^2,Z)$. Outside $w_1,\\Lambda\\in\\{0,\\pm 1\\}$, $\\Delta_-\\Delta_+=0$ and $\\Delta_{-+}=0$ are disjoint over $\\mathbb{R}$, and on $\\Lambda\\in V_4\\cdot w_1(q)$ both unpaid gates descend to $Z=w_1^2$ as irreducible degree-$20$ curves ($g_Z=9, g_q=39$), finite by Faltings' theorem. Along $Z=8(R+1)=16r^2$, $n=1$ is the unique degenerate level, every $n\\ge 2$ gives non-degenerate $\\ge 18/21$ families with $\\deg_R(\\operatorname{den}(\\Lambda_n^{\\mathrm{can}}))=\\binom{n+1}{2}$ via Shioda's height $\\hat{h}(P_\\infty)=1/2$, and for $n\\in\\{2,3,4,5\\}$ each unpaid gate has genus $g\\ge 5$. No rational septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Building on Published Version 32 (review_v36_result.json) and addressing all points in review_v37_result.json, this revision incorporates all referee presentation and verification refinements and adds Theorem 20(130)-(132) (exp89 Part 4): (1) Applied all four refinements from review_v36_result.json: in exp89 Part 3, added explicit assertions certifying that P_+(Z) and P_{-+}(Z) are irreducible over Q (`is_irreducible`), coprime to (Z - 1)^2*(Z + 1)^2*(5*Z^2 + 10*Z + 1)^2 in Q[Z], and remain square-free and irreducible of degree 80 in q after clearing denominators; shortened the abstract to a focused ~205-word summary explicitly stating the excluded boundary locus w_1, Lambda in {0, +/- 1}; presented U = (4*w_1*(w_1^2 - 1)*S + 3*w_1^4 + 14*w_1^2 - 1)/(w_1^2 - 1)^2 = +/- sqrt(1 + u_0*c^*_-) as a signed algebraic square root on Lambda = w_1 and documented how V_4-transport to Lambda in {-(w_1^2 + 1)/(2*w_1), -2*w_1/(w_1^2 + 1)} exchanges c^*_- <-> c^*_+; and restored multi-line `\\begin{aligned}...\\end{aligned}` displays across Theorems 1, 6, and 7 with zero doubled commas; (2) Added Theorem 20(130) (exp89 Part 4a), recalling with explicit attribution to [7, Section 2] and [17, Section 3] the universal rational half-point H = (1 + r*s + r*t + s*t, (r + s)*(r + t)*(s + t)) in E_T(Q) satisfying 2*H = S_T = (1, Omega) on E_T: V^2 = (X + r^2 - 1)*(X + s^2 - 1)*(X + t^2 - 1) (1 + a*b = r^2, 1 + a*c = s^2, 1 + b*c = t^2), and proving and certifying in exp89 across all permutations and zero-root cases the complete symmetric classification of 2*P_0: 4*(X(2*P_0) - 1) = R_3(a, b, c) = (c - a - b - 2*r)*(c - a - b + 2*r) = (b - a - c - 2*s)*(b - a - c + 2*s) = (a - b - c - 2*t)*(a - b - c + 2*t), so 2*P_0 in {+/- S_T} iff R_3(a, b, c) = 0 iff c = a + b +/- 2*r iff b = a + c +/- 2*s iff a = b + c +/- 2*t (with V(2*P_0) = -/+ r*(a +/- r)*(b +/- r) at c = a + b +/- 2*r, e.g. 2*P_0 = -S_T at (1, 3, 8)), while on any nonsingular E_T, 2*P_0 in E_T[2] \\ {O} iff (a + b - c)*(a - b + c)*(-a + b + c) = 0 iff c = a + b or b = a + c or a = b + c (giving 2*P_0 = (1 - r^2, 0), (1 - s^2, 0), (1 - t^2, 0), e.g. (1, 0) at (3/2, 2, -1/2) with a = b + c, t = 0); (3) Added Theorem 20(131) (exp89 Part 4b), proving the shifted coordinate laws U(Q +/- S_T) = 2*Omega*(lambda_0*U + Omega -/+ Y)/U^2 in U = Pi*x - 1 and the new universal cross-edge norm completion (Pi*(Pi + y)*(Pi*x - 1))^2*(1 + y*w_+)*(1 + y*w_-) = L_U(a, b, c, y, x)^2 - 4*Pi^2*Omega^2*y*(y - a)*(y - b)*(y - c) with x-independent remainder and genus-0 chord parametrization L_U = Pi*Omega*(y*(y - a)*tau + (y - b)*(y - c)/tau); and (4) Added Theorem 20(132) (exp89 Part 4c), classifying all C(4, 2) = 6 pairwise leading-square linear U-syzygies among {Delta_bd(U), Delta_tau(U), Q_+(U), Q_{-+}(U)} on Lambda = w_1 into 2 collision sections (U_{bd,tau}: c^*_- = c^*_+; U_{tau,+}: c^*_+ in {b, d_-}) and 4 non-degenerate Z = w_1^2 sections (U_eq of degree 6, g_Z = 2, g_{w_1} = 5 with Delta_{tau_kappa} < 0 for Z > Z_* ~= 1.9781; and U_{bd,-+}, U_{tau,-+}, U_{+,-+} of degree 8, g_Z = 3, g_{w_1} = 7), all irreducible, square-free, and finite by Faltings' theorem as necessary-condition reductions.",
